[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded Generated Frontend Simulation Bridge

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-BRIDGE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Atomic operating-point request elaboration
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall optionally lower constant DC R/V/I primitives and active subcircuit instances into the existing typed operating-point request. It shall preserve signed sources, parameter scope and overrides, ordered port bindings, private-node isolation and source/instance provenance. Unsupported active cards, invalid values, ambiguous or deferred bindings, recursion and exceeded expansion budgets shall refuse the whole request without publishing partial circuits. Syntax acceptance alone shall never imply simulation support.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: PrimitiveSyntax.cs, ParameterEvaluator.EvaluateValue and OperatingPointBridge.cs. Verification: BridgeTests, FsCheck seed 901,20261101, Stryker.NET bridge stage and scripts/QualifyOperatingPointBridge.cs. Initial limits: depth 32, 128 expansion frames including root, 1024 elements and 128 nodes. Only literal 0 is ground. A globally definite catalog is required, including declaration uncertainty in unused bodies. Model devices, waveform sources, AC/transient, controls and general ngspice conformance remain outside this bridge profile. Existing Rust solver functionality is unchanged.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-PARAM-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-REBIN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Opt-in corpus resource rebinding evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Corpus qualification shall optionally resolve resources under explicitly permitted roots and report resolution and expanded semantic binding separately from original syntax acceptance and simulation support. Refused resources shall retain diagnostic codes without presenting missing expanded semantics as successful binding. Default syntax-only corpus operation shall perform no resource access or simulation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Run-SyntaxCorpus.ps1 ResourceRoots and Simulator.Syntax.Corpus ResourceProfileObserver. The existing strict UTF-8, file/depth/byte and denied-link policies apply. Evidence shall identify exact source hashes, roots, completed and unavailable rows. This observation profile does not execute the accepted corpus.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-RESOURCE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-EVIDENCE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Separate syntax acceptance from numerical comparison evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Each completed corpus gap checkpoint shall record fresh ngspice numerical comparisons separately from syntax, resource resolution and binding counts. Numerical reports shall identify their importer or frontend path, tested source and executable identities, unique fully compared files, partially compared files, mismatches, explicit refusals and unfinished inputs. Named generated fixtures and repeated solver executions shall not inflate corpus file counts. Performance claims shall use comparable analyses and build profiles with repeated measurements, separately from correctness comparisons.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
User-requested reporting contract. Implementation uses the existing CorpusCommand numerical matrix and QualifyOperatingPointBridge named DC regression, independently of the generated syntax corpus. TABLE recognition alone does not add Rust interpolation support. Raw artifacts belong to the explicit campaign output; benchmark raw artifacts follow an explicit report parent. Draft pending this checkpoint's actual verification evidence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-BRIDGE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-SELECT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit linear static operating-point selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall provide an explicit selected static operating-point operation for ideal R/C/L and independent constant V/I declarations, preserving the strict R/V/I Lower operation. Every excluded analysis, input control program or supported read-only observation shall be reported with scope, original source range, leading token and reason. Input controls shall never execute. Unqualified physical/directive semantics shall remain refused, including potentially global effects in unused bodies. R/C/L values shall be finite and strictly positive in SI units. Failed preparation shall return no partial request, origins or omission plan.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Bounded implementation: OperatingPointSelection.Select; OperatingPointBridge.LowerSelected/LowerCore; generated ScopedCard.Name metadata. Verification: SelectedOperatingPointTests including replay 907,20261101, physical directive red regression and zero-inductance mutation follow-up; FrontendCorpusIntegration compares original-source native operating points. No original AC/transient/control program or model-device execution is implied. Default Lower remains unchanged.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-BRIDGE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-EXEC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Actual generated-frontend corpus execution outcomes
STATEMENT: >>>
An opt-in qualification harness shall run supported generated-frontend requests through the public typed wire boundary to existing CPU solvers. It shall retain input/resource/source/binary fingerprints and hash-pinned exclusions, verify the actual root read against the inventory identity, distinguish preparation refusal, provider failure, completed solve, reference unavailability and numerical agreement, and count unique input files separately from provider runs and fixture campaigns. Successful provider data shall match the requested case/provider identity, finite sample and unique signal contracts and required voltage units. A failed provider result shall not suppress the other provider's evidence. Configurable bounded admission and child-process budgets shall leave unfinished work explicit.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Run-FrontendCorpus.cs. Verification: real corpus replay plus FrontendCorpusIntegration and synthetic FrontendResultFaultIntegration. Synthetic protocol faults are never simulator qualification. Admission is checked between inputs; bounded current-row operations may finish after it. Missing root observables are unavailable, not zero or a numerical discrepancy. Source changes before finalization prevent a completed report. New source/helper fingerprint and elapsed/UTC metadata supplement the reused Rust executable identity.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-EVIDENCE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEM-ORACLE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent selected operating-point reference precision
STATEMENT: >>>
Selected operating-point qualification shall compare root-node voltages against native ngspice from the independently expanded original source, preserving device/parameter values. Only explicitly recorded generated source ranges may be excluded from the oracle's original control, analysis and observation instructions. The oracle shall use sufficient printed precision without increasing the declared numerical bound to hide formatting discrepancies. Missing, non-finite, duplicate or otherwise unavailable reference observations shall not count as numerical passes. Absent root observables shall remain explicitly unqualified even when solvers complete.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Run-FrontendCorpus.cs AST-located projection, 17-digit print probes and explicit absolute 1e-9 V plus relative 1e-8 bound. Actual echo interpolation rounded a repeating-fraction case to six digits; precision-control experiment and red fraction regression establish why print replaces echo. Zero-port and malformed-response red regressions retain unavailable versus mismatch distinctions. Only root-node voltages are compared; internal nodes, source currents and complete original programs remain outside this profile.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-EXEC-001
